  "Notes": "Three-layer quarter-wave beam divider\nSpecification: All layers quarter-wave at 550 nm.\nReported: Table p. 338: R = 61.0 %, T = 38.0 % at 550 nm.\nNotes: Paper lists from the glass outward (SiO on glass, TiO2 on top); reversed here. 'MgF' in the table is MgF2. SiO taken as true SiO, nD = 1.97 (footnote p. 338); the footnote warns slower deposition or oxygen gives much lower n, and an ideal calculation with n = 1.97 gives about 66.8 %, above the printed 61 %, so the SiO films were probably of lower index or slightly absorbing.\nLayers from Table on p. 338 (row 'SiO - MgF - TiO2'); layer 1 faces the incident medium.\nChecked with ThinFilmDesigner (2026-10-21), compare with the paper: ours R 66.8 % at 550 nm; paper R 61 % (measured, table p. 338). The paper’s SiO index (1.97, true SiO) is used; its own footnote says evaporated SiO films often come out lower, which would bring R down towards the measured value.",
